            "review_title": "Review at Jollibee - Vincom Center Da Nang",
            "review_text": "ste\n4 contributions\n0\nWE ARE SAD FILIPINOS\nApr 2019 • Family\nWe were in Vietnam for 2 weeks. On our past night we craved for Jollibee and we were so excited. First the menu is entirely different from what we have in the Philippimes. Nothing is the same except for the chicken and spaghetti. The drinks are different too. I understand that this is made for the Vietnamese taste. Everything was just ok but it's not a real Jollibee. It feels like a new restaurant with just the same trade name. I was hoping that the chicken would be as good as the real jollibee in the Philippines but it's not at all the same. I felt so sad being a Filipino that what the Vietnamese thinks their having is Jollibee but its not. Jollibee Vietnam should at least measure up to the real chcken. They changed the menu but at least have the chicken taste like Jollibee's. The spag taste a bit thr same but still different. I hope the Vietnamese and other nationalities won't think that this is what Jollibee is like. I am telling you, it's not. Please do something about this. It can ruin the name of Jollibee and its reputation.\nRead more\nWritten April 26, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
