            "review_text": "elizabethlavanza55\nCaracas, Venezuela1 contribution\n1\nAdequate experience, except for the dining experience at Sumo BBQ\nDec 2017 • Family\nThe place itself was quite modern, spacious and well kept. Despite this, the one horrible experience that disappointed the whole trip was Sumo BBQ. The restaurant emanates of rotten anchovies that nearly made my sister nauseous enough to vomit after being exposed to the pungent odour for only 2 minutes. After we were given a table they immediately told us that they are not going to provide us napkins! I genuinely thought the waiter (who could barely understand a word) was joking but he was dead serious... The meat itself was like excess rubber that is used for the manufacturing of the motorcycle's tyres seen outside the streets. Additionally, the order for rice never came and they almost charged my family for it! Both the food and service was appalling as the waiter (the same one aforementioned) swiftly snatched the money straight out of my hands and counted the money as if he didn't trust us! I recommend you to avoid this restaurant like the Black plague itself as I would have been more satisfied munching on dog food in the sewers of Da Nang than dining at Sumo BBQ!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten December 22, 2017",
